LOGBOOK.md:10:- MEASUREMENT: Corrected exact-tree loopback probes ran 100/500/1000 real HEV cycles. Post-warmup net change was `+81,944 B` / `-212,992 B` / `-32,768 B`; maximum drawup was `98,328 B` / `65,536 B` / `65,536 B`; increase/equal/decrease transitions were `3/85/1`, `4/479/6`, and `7/977/5`. The prior late approximately 16 KiB jumps above cycle 1000 disappeared; the last 1000-cycle increase was cycle 481. Every sample restored live sessions, reads, and queues to zero; descriptors ended at 3 and threads at 8.
LOGBOOK.md:11:- RULE: A fresh production-entry repeat proved 100 cycles insufficient: it stopped fail-closed on one `+65,536 B` increase and no release. The simplest repeatable gate therefore uses the next predeclared row, 500 cycles, after fixed 10-sample warmup. It permits a full plateau or a measured release only while maximum drawup stays within 256 KiB (1% of the upper 25 MiB target); late unreleased rise and a released-but-over-ceiling linear sawtooth fail closed. The earlier 2000-cycle/trailing-1000 rule measured observer allocation and is retired rather than widened further.
LOGBOOK.md:14:- INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 2000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. The sampler observed both rises and releases, including `-1,196,032 B` and `-1,130,496 B` segments; post-warmup net change was `-2,310,120 B`. Across the last 500 samples, net change was `-65,536 B` and range was `98,304 B`. Descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed within `6...8`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. Earlier 500- and 1000-cycle repeats still had late rises, proving neither duration alone established convergence.
LOGBOOK.md:15:- RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 2000 samples (20× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, post-warmup and trailing 1000-sample maximum drawup no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope), and either a trailing plateau or an observed post-warmup release. Maximum drawup measures each upward excursion from the running minimum, so a large release is not itself a failure. Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive plateau and bounded-oscillation tests plus unreleased late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
LOGBOOK.md:16:- ANOMALY/FIX: The first extended attempt stopped at cycle 257 with Swift signal 5 because the test payload used checked `UInt8(iteration)`. `UInt8(truncatingIfNeeded:)` removes that artificial 255-cycle harness limit while address and port continue to identify each flow. The 2000-cycle investigation passed in 106.74 seconds. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.
LOGBOOK.md:19:- FIX: The physical-matrix entry now independently computes the actual working candidate tree with a task-local temporary Git index and rejects a well-formed forged `RELUX_CANDIDATE_TREE_OID` before HEV work or evidence emission. It independently hashes the linked macOS HEV archive against the pinned manifest. Negative production-call-site coverage rejects forged tree and artifact hashes.
LOGBOOK.md:20:- RULE: Lifecycle analysis uses an explicit fixed 10-sample allocator warmup. Across the remaining 90 samples it classifies any non-decreasing sequence with at least one increase as monotonic growth and records warmup/window/net-change plus increase/equal/decrease transition counts. Pure negative coverage flags rise-plus-plateau and accepts a plateau stabilized after warmup.
LOGBOOK.md:21:- STOP: Three independent 100-cycle physical-Mac probes all failed the corrected gate: `+81,920 B` with `4/85/0`, `+81,920 B` with `5/84/0`, and `+98,328 B` with `4/85/0` increase/equal/decrease transitions. Per rev3 instructions, the 100/250/500 matrix and full suite were not run against a known failing lifecycle prerequisite, and the rule was not weakened. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.
LOGBOOK.md:24:- MEASUREMENT: A physical Mac15,9 (arm64, macOS 26.5) SwiftPM run admitted 100, 250, and the explicitly narrowed 500-session ceiling with zero bridge drops. Physical footprint was 12,354,160 B, 15,270,512 B, and 20,038,256 B; peak was 20,054,640 B. The incremental 500-session HEV/bridge cost was 11,976,704 B, leaving 19,480,576 B inside the provisional 30 MiB envelope. This is not a whole-extension Apple guarantee and does not allocate SSH, DNS, relay, caches, or reconnect overlap.
LOGBOOK.md:25:- LIFECYCLE: One hundred real HEV start/traffic/stop cycles restored descriptors, sessions, queued batches, outstanding reads, boundary start/stop ownership, and HEV/bridge close stages; sampled physical footprint did not grow monotonically. Seven startup and seven cleanup cancellation stages plus 50 harness host-termination iterations passed.
