LOGBOOK.md:289:- REWORK: The race now signals cancellation before resuming its caller. The bounded ownership registry supports count-targeted retirement waiters, and a timed-out upload gives cooperative children at most 250 ms of the injected close budget to reconcile while permitting exactly one additional operation—the cancellation-ignoring source—to remain visible until release. The regression uses bounded monotonic state synchronization and fails instead of hanging if ownership cannot settle.
LOGBOOK.md:332:- REWORK: Socket-service cancellation now retires only its independently cancellable readiness operation. Channel opens may queue behind rekey under their original bounded deadline. One bounded shared rekey flight coalesces trigger reasons and lets a canceled caller detach while KEX continues. Per-channel FIFO gates retain exact write arguments across `EAGAIN`, with queued bytes still reserved against the caller cap. Returned credential algorithms must belong to both adapter capabilities and the request allowlist.
LOGBOOK.md:333:- CONFORMANCE: Deterministic loopback regressions prove canceled and timed-out reads leave sibling channels and the session ready; an open times out while rekey is deliberately suspended and a second queued open succeeds afterward; two rekey triggers produce one KEX while the first caller cancels; four concurrent same-channel payloads survive forced bridge backpressure byte-exactly; and a supported-but-disallowed credential algorithm fails before authentication.
LOGBOOK.md:338:- REWORK: A bounded FIFO session-operation gate now holds one permit across every channel-open, client-rekey, and keepalive/global-request `EAGAIN` sequence while independent channel payload I/O remains interleavable. Callback would-block paths return `-EAGAIN`. Timeout adaptation uses structured tasks and joins the losing branch; bridge shutdown marks terminal state, closes the injected connection, cancels and joins every queued service task, and only then discards buffers or frees engine state.
LOGBOOK.md:344:- REWORK: Socket progress now has one queued owner with exact-once partial drains. Channel reads enforce one pending operation per stream, writes reserve against the per-channel queued-byte cap, all pending gauges are live, and cancel/reset/close marks disposition then waits for tracked pointer users before bounded free. Session/open/connect teardown paths similarly drain active owners and serialize concurrent teardown.
