LOGBOOK.md:721:- REWORK: Domain sends now reserve socketless association capacity and an exact generation/incarnation token before resolver admission. A fixed worker pool and fixed queued-job/completion credit bound copied names, payloads, inspected/accepted results, retained result bytes, deadlines, and concurrent lookups; `Send` returns `pendingResolution` without blocking the event-loop caller. Completion attaches a family socket only through the original token.
LOGBOOK.md:722:- LIFECYCLE: Registry retirement cancels an incarnation-local context on close, idle expiry, generation replacement, session loss, process shutdown, or parent cancellation. Active and queued jobs recheck that context before resolver/socket work, and token-scoped socket admission prevents a paused old lookup from reopening or sending through a same-generation reused ID. Deterministic barriers restore job, queue, name, payload, result, completion, worker, association, timer, socket, and descriptor counts to their declared baselines.
LOGBOOK.md:735:- RESOLVER/FAIRNESS: Domain use validates the accepted ASCII presentation form (including numeric-text and malformed A-label rejection) before a cancellable resolver seam. Concurrent requests, deadline, inspected result count, copied result bytes, family selection, turn targets, socket visits, datagrams, bytes, and monotonic time all have immutable checked caps. The inspected-result cap is independent of accepted results, so invalid resolver output cannot force an unbounded scan. Names, addresses, payloads, and raw resolver/socket errors never enter diagnostics or metric dimensions.
LOGBOOK.md:745:- IMPLEMENTATION: A single Go owner goroutine now linearizes relay association admission, descriptor use, activity, close, expiry, generation replacement, and cancellation. Identity is the session generation plus nonzero client association ID plus a monotonically increasing local incarnation, so stale timer/activity/close work cannot affect a reused numeric ID.
LOGBOOK.md:746:- RESOURCE POLICY: Association, family-specific socket, logical timer, and pending-close credits are checked before descriptor creation and report finite aggregate counters. One indexed deadline heap and one physical monotonic timer bound timer/task state; expiry events consume reserved pending-close credit until observed. IPv4 and IPv6 descriptors are created lazily and closed exactly once across normal, partial-failure, expiry, session, process, and cancellation paths.
